# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: a header defining a constant as `_Pragma("clang diagnostic
# ignored \"-Wsign-conversion\"") 5` and binding it beside `abs(x: u32)`:
# the constant's return assertion expanded the macro above the probes, and
# the sign check was off for them; it built and printed `10`.
#
# CAUSE: a `_Pragma` stands where the macro is expanded, on the compiler's
# own line, after the groups' includes.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-a-constant-s-pragma-turns-off-no-check.h"
    constant QUIET_FIVE: i32
    function abs(x: u32) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(abs(5) + QUIET_FIVE)
